<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ralph Moor</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1860–1909</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir Ralph Moor was a British colonial administrator who served as commissioner of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> Coast <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">Protectorate</a> from 1896 and then as the first high commissioner of the Protectorate of Southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> from 1900 to 1903. He organised the punitive expedition of 1897 that sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-city">Benin City</a> and ended the independence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ralph-moor.jpg" alt="Ralph Moor" width="320" height="349" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ralph_Denham_Rayment_Moor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
